  ov_p_more: '{0} records added · {1} name decisions · {2} reading corrections · {3} QA hints · {4} unsure', ov_how: 'How it works',
  ov_how_body: `<ol><li><b>Choose a queue</b> (tiles above or the list on the left): start with “Machine findings” — entries in which a scan check calls records wrong, spurious or missing. The list starts with the most severe findings; the level chips (severe / medium / minor) narrow it down.</li>
<li><b>Compare card and scan:</b> the focused card marks the record's line on the scan (wheel = zoom, drag = pan, double-click = fit the entry).</li>
<li><b>Decide:</b> <kbd>J</kbd> apply / confirm (reading correction: the better reading) · <kbd>K</kbd> the machine's correction stands · <kbd>N</kbd> is right / revert · <kbd>E</kbd> edit · <kbd>X</kbd> strike · <kbd>U</kbd> unsure · <kbd>↑</kbd> <kbd>↓</kbd> card · <kbd>Z</kbd> undo.</li>
<li><b>Entry checked</b> (<kbd>⏎</kbd> on the last card): records without a decision count as right. <kbd>→</kbd> next entry of the list.</li>
<li><b>Save &amp; export:</b> ZIP with the files for <code>data/review/</code>. Name decisions apply to all entries.</li></ol>`,
