  help: `<h2>Graph check · Laubmann Knowledge Graph</h2>
<p>The page shows the exported graph (every triple) entry by entry, next to the scan and everything machines changed or objected to. None of it has been checked by a human so far.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Left</b> the work list: queues with the number of open entries, below them the level filter (severe / medium / minor, combinable), volume filter, sorting (default: most severe findings first). Per entry: coloured numbers = open findings per level, ¶ = text insert, ▣ = image/map/object, ✓ = checked.</li>
<li><b>Middle</b> the subgraph. Ring and badge of a node carry the <b>gravity in the colour</b> (red severe · orange medium · yellow minor · grey-blue hint) and the <b>kind in the marker</b>: <b>!</b> finding of a check · <b>M</b> changed automatically · <b>?</b> suggestion or missing record · <b>×</b> removed · green <b>✓</b> decided by you. The layer <i>Properties</i> writes every statement of a node into its box (compact with many records: one line, everything on the selected node and in the tooltip); <i>Show everything</i> switches every layer on. The pill on a record gives its estimated error risk. <kbd>G</kbd> switches to the records table (every property as a column, “Columns ▾”; click a cell = edit, chip “is → should be” = accept the proposal).</li>
<li><b>Right</b> the scan with the entry's regions (dashed + “approximate” = estimated), the outlines of its images and inserts (violet; click opens the card) and the line of the selected record; below it the tabs <i>Check</i> (cards by gravity: severe, medium, minor, then the hints, collapsed), <i>Text</i> (reading corrections in the text, own text correction) and <i>Node</i> (all triples).</li>
<li><b>Keys:</b> <kbd>J</kbd> apply/confirm (reading correction: the better reading) · <kbd>K</kbd> the machine's correction stands · <kbd>N</kbd> is right/revert/old text · <kbd>E</kbd> edit · <kbd>X</kbd> strike the record · <kbd>U</kbd> unsure · <kbd>↑</kbd> <kbd>↓</kbd> card · <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd> entry in the list · <kbd>⏎</kbd> on the last card = entry checked · <kbd>Z</kbd> undo · <kbd>S</kbd> scan · <kbd>G</kbd> graph/table · <kbd>/</kbd> search · <kbd>Esc</kbd> close a form.</li>
<li><b>Reliability</b> (bar below the header, in every view): measure (whole record, occurrence, place, observer, coordinates) and threshold of the estimated error risk (all, &lt; 50 %, &lt; 25 %, &lt; 10 %), with the number of records shown and how many of them are probably wrong. The filter is a view only: graph, table, work list, node and class views and all numbers show these records only; decisions and export always cover everything. “show n outside” brings the other records of an entry back, dimmed. The queue <i>By error risk</i> orders the entries by the expected number of wrong records.</li>
<li><b>Name decisions</b> (species, place, person, habitat) apply to the name in ALL entries. A georeference finding concerns the place: here only “this record only”, otherwise the link page.</li>
<li><b>Save &amp; export</b>: the state lives in the browser and in a backup file; the ZIP holds the files for <code>data/review/</code>. The graph only changes at the next pipeline run.</li>
</ul>`,
